* indirect_dispatch -- sums add1(1..500) through APPLY(<name held in a variable>, arg).
* bottleneck: by-name dispatch to a program-defined target; contrast with func_call (direct) and eval_fixed (EVAL).
        DEFINE('add1(v)')                               :(add1_end)
add1    add1 = v + 1                                    :(RETURN)
add1_end fname = 'add1'
        sum = 0
        i = 1
loop    sum = sum + APPLY(fname, i)
        i = LT(i, 500) i + 1                            :S(loop)
        OUTPUT = 'sum of add1(1..500) through APPLY = ' sum
END
